1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,880
Hello, Kawajiri residence.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:04,830
Huh?

3
00:00:04,913 --> 00:00:06,405
No, you have the wrong number.

4
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,700
Superb work, Hayato.

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:13,220
You've kept that meddlesome Rohan at bay.

6
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,377
I dare say you're a chip
right off the old block.

7
00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:18,697
Like I said, you've got the wrong number.

8
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:19,610
Goodbye.

9
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:22,037
I'm proud of you, boy.

10
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:25,657
Now I have even more reason to
provide for my beautiful family.

11
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:27,799
But first, the adults need to talk.

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,860
Honey Bunch, I'd love a
goodbye kiss before I leave.

13
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,320
What are you doing, Hayato?

14
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:51,149
That's my expensive china!

15
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:53,297
Why would you do that?

16
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:54,337
What's wrong with you?

17
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:57,177
I never know what's going on
inside that head of yours!

18
00:00:57,260 --> 00:01:00,400
You act like you don't hear
me, and I don't know why!

19
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:02,840
Where did I go wrong?

20
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,340
You can't see it yet, Mom,
but he's a murderous psycho.

21
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:15,640
If I tell anyone about him,

22
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:19,417
the listener will explode and
time will reset to this morning.

23
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:21,265
It may not happen for a while,

24
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:24,197
but if we keep letting him
have free reign over our lives,

25
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:25,751
eventually he'll kill us.

26
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:46,382
But luckily for me, I now know about someone
else who has special powers like Kira!

27
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:47,820
Rohan Kishibe!

28
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:50,337
I have to find a way
to talk to him somehow!

29
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:52,397
I have to get him to help me or we don't

30
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:55,068
stand a ghost of a
chance of defeating Kira!

31
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:01,795
Rohan's already here!

32
00:02:02,860 --> 00:02:06,331
If I approach him directly,
he'll get blown to smithereens.

33
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:09,265
Then I'll be forced to
relive the same morning.

34
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:13,444
I've got to tell Rohan the info
without meeting him face to face.

35
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:15,360
It's time to change fate.

36
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:20,320
What? What?

37
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:21,440
My face!

38
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:22,640
What's going on?

39
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:24,310
Hang on!

40
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:27,539
Rohan did this to me when
we met that other morning!

41
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,150
Damn it.

42
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:35,057
But I've been keeping out
of sight this entire time.

43
00:02:35,140 --> 00:02:37,493
There's no way Rohan could have seen me.

44
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,740
Once the wheels of fate are set in
motion, there's no turning them back.

45
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:45,310
Hayato.

46
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:49,550
Hayato.

47
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:08,560
Breakdown, Breakdown Breakdown, Breakdown

48
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:16,757
Let the voice of love take you

49
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:29,697
Let the joy of love give her a

50
00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:34,197
dance on My care and the love of

51
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:38,437
love give her a dance on Let the

52
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:40,977
joy of love give her a

53
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:47,700
dance on

54
00:04:10,580 --> 00:04:11,410
Breakdown!

55
00:04:11,493 --> 00:04:12,323
Come on!

56
00:04:12,406 --> 00:04:15,301
The weather report never
said anything about rain!

57
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:21,717
I'm sure you would like
to believe you shattered

58
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:24,597
your mother's favorite
teapot of your own free will.

59
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:25,798
But you'd be wrong.

60
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:31,121
You simply experienced a reoccurrence of
the pot breaking from the previous morning.

61
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:33,140
It's preordained, son.

62
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:37,097
That's how fate works,
as you're about to learn.

63
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:42,004
If Rohan transformed you into a book the
morning before, then a book you shall be.

64
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:45,757
That is what makes Deadly Queen's
Bites the Dust unstoppable.

65
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:49,800
It reverses time and nullifies
the exposure of my identity.

66
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:54,317
Which means I'll have the
pleasure of watching Rohan

67
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:58,100
explode into obsolescence and
still make it to work on time.

68
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:01,190
No!

69
00:05:01,273 --> 00:05:02,540
I can't let Rohan die!

70
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:06,400
I have to go save him
before it's too late!

71
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:24,380
Poor Rohan Kishibe.

72
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:28,000
Now watch carefully.

73
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:32,401
The fool has absolutely no idea
why he's about to breathe his last.

74
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:37,908
But I'm sure he's realized that his life
as a manga artist has come to an end.

75
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:47,300
Eichi!

76
00:05:57,700 --> 00:06:00,160
No, not Rohan!

77
00:06:03,420 --> 00:06:06,260
Oh God, why?

78
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:13,190
Hi, Ito.

79
00:06:13,420 --> 00:06:16,377
Your visit with Rohan is
now as if it never happened,

80
00:06:16,460 --> 00:06:19,166
and the morning will go
on as it always would.

81
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:22,660
Of course, I could undo
Bites the Dust right now,

82
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:26,117
which means that Rohan's death would
become a permanent temporal point.

83
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:28,617
But for now, I think
I'll let it do its thing.

84
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:32,171
I suspect a few of his cohorts
will be dropping by shortly.

85
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:37,177
When they do you're going to make me a
proud papa by exterminating the lot of them?

86
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:39,900
You're my own personal landmine!

87
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:42,420
But chin up

88
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:45,417
as long as you're a good little
secret weapon bites the dust

89
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:49,400
won't harm you So relax and
do whatever you schoolboys do

90
00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:56,140
Well daddy's off to the station
no slacking at school now!

91
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:03,757
This is only happening because
he crossed paths with me!

92
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:05,457
It's my fault!

93
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:07,940
He met me and got murdered for it.

94
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:20,420
What now?

95
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:24,080
Isn't there anything I can
do to stop this monster?

96
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:32,920
Pardon me, can I ask you a question?

97
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:36,460
Would you happen to have the time?

98
00:07:36,980 --> 00:07:39,686
My stupid watch seems
to be out of commission.

99
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:42,100
Hello in there, anyone home?

100
00:07:46,020 --> 00:07:47,900
Yeah, it's 8.33.

101
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:51,793
You know, I have this weird
feeling I've seen you before.

102
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,180
Now, where was it?

103
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:56,384
You wouldn't happen to
know who I am, would you?

104
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:57,590
No.

105
00:07:57,673 --> 00:07:58,940
Oh well, my mistake.

106
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:02,011
I hope I didn't weird you out or anything.

107
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:04,120
But now I know it's 8.33.

108
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:05,590
Thanks!

109
00:08:06,760 --> 00:08:07,760
Mr. Jotaro!

110
00:08:08,020 --> 00:08:09,680
Looks like it is after 8.30.

111
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:10,940
How strange.

112
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:12,797
Rohan sensei knew we were coming.

113
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:13,710
Where'd he go?

114
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:16,460
These are Rohan Kishibe's friends!

115
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:18,033
They plan to meet here!

116
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:21,606
They must have the same
kind of powers as him!

117
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:25,565
So I bet they all came here to
question me about Yoshikage Kira!

118
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:33,760
No, no, no, no, no!

119
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,997
If they figure out I'm Hayato Kawajiri
and start interrogating me about Dad,

120
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,433
it's all over for them!

121
00:08:44,060 --> 00:08:45,337
Sorry about that, kid.

122
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:48,357
I was looking for my friends and I'm
still kind of groggy from oversleeping.

123
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:50,337
I know I've seen this kid's face before,

124
00:08:50,420 --> 00:08:53,185
but for the life of me,
I can't remember where.

125
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:55,050
Hey, look!

126
00:08:55,180 --> 00:08:56,592
It's Josuke and Okuyasu!

127
00:08:56,980 --> 00:08:57,810
What's up, bro?

128
00:08:57,893 --> 00:08:58,723
Yo, Koichi!

129
00:08:58,806 --> 00:09:00,977
Hope your morning's been spiffy, Jotaro!

130
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:02,940
Th-there are two more of them!

131
00:09:03,820 --> 00:09:06,797
Kira told me that others would
eventually be showing up!

132
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:08,460
He was talking about them!

133
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:11,584
...the kid's house without
Rohan helping us out.

134
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:15,216
Sorry, I nearly forgot I was
still hanging on to this.

135
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:16,772
I believe this is yours.

136
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:20,280
Oh, thanks a lot.

137
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:23,042
You know, it might be the angle.

138
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:25,020
Oh yeah, I'm sure of it.

139
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:27,400
I know I've seen that face before.

140
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:31,800
I don't know from where, but he
looks too familiar to be a stranger.

141
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:35,400
Koichi, look at the name
on his backpack. Huh?

142
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:38,760
Hi, it's Okawajiri! What?

143
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,860
Crap, they figured me out!

144
00:09:54,620 --> 00:09:57,780
Hayato Kawajiri, what the
hell are you doing here?

145
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:59,440
Was all this planned?

146
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:03,254
Wait, could this have something
to do with Rohan-sensei?

147
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:05,886
What am I supposed to do now?

148
00:10:06,140 --> 00:10:09,337
If these guys start questioning
me about my dad, it's all over!

149
00:10:09,420 --> 00:10:11,596
The bomb will kill every one of them!

150
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:16,075
No, please don't ask me any questions!

151
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:21,136
If you guys end up getting killed,
who's gonna get rid of the murderer?

152
00:10:22,060 --> 00:10:24,300
If I have to dupe them, then so be it.

153
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:26,940
Whatever it takes, I can't let them die.

154
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:32,120
I'd like to ask you about this photo.

155
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:36,937
To be more precise, I want to know the
reason behind your video recording.

156
00:10:37,020 --> 00:10:38,400
Be straight with me.

157
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:41,200
Why were you... Shoot! Nosebleed!

158
00:10:41,740 --> 00:10:42,570
Oh no!

159
00:10:42,653 --> 00:10:44,917
I don't know why my nose
started bleeding out of nowhere,

160
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,757
but I have to find a doctor, sorry!

161
00:10:46,840 --> 00:10:47,670
Hold it!

162
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:50,177
You said you got a nosebleed, huh?

163
00:10:50,260 --> 00:10:51,090
Let's see it.

164
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:55,340
Come on, let me see.

165
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:58,550
It's bad.

166
00:10:58,700 --> 00:10:59,800
I need a doctor.

167
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:02,241
Nah, I don't think it's that bad.

168
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:05,170
See?

169
00:11:05,253 --> 00:11:06,453
It's not even bleeding.

170
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:13,457
Josuke Higashikata, nice to meet you.

171
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:14,800
That's Jotaro Kujo.

172
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,176
one of my relatives.

173
00:11:16,460 --> 00:11:18,980
Derp face over there is Okuyasu Nijimura.

174
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:22,102
And that's Koichi Hirosei,
the nicest guy I know.

175
00:11:22,420 --> 00:11:26,891
You go to Budogaoka Elementary, so
you've got some time before class starts.

176
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,059
We won't take up much of your time.

177
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:30,972
Now, about this picture.

178
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:34,600
If it's nothing, we'll just be on our way.

179
00:11:35,020 --> 00:11:38,432
It is something, but I can't
answer any of your questions.

180
00:11:39,180 --> 00:11:40,420
Please don't ask.

181
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:42,644
You see the man you're filming?

182
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:44,897
Would he happen to be your dad?

183
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:45,810
I'm begging you!

184
00:11:45,893 --> 00:11:47,192
Don't say anything else!

185
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:52,910
Crap.

186
00:11:52,993 --> 00:11:53,823
What have I done?

187
00:11:54,060 --> 00:11:56,707
Now they're going to
ask even more questions.

188
00:11:58,020 --> 00:12:00,337
What do you mean, don't say anything else?

189
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:01,437
They're not gonna stop.

190
00:12:01,520 --> 00:12:03,237
Just what is it that we shouldn't say?

191
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:04,737
There's nothing I can do!

192
00:12:04,820 --> 00:12:06,577
Does all of this have to do with your dad?

193
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:08,072
The bomb's gonna go off!

194
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:09,631
It's gonna kill them all!

195
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:12,920
What the hell's going on, huh?

196
00:12:13,060 --> 00:12:14,884
Why can't we say anything else?

197
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,477
Yeah, I mean, we haven't
even asked him anything yet.

198
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:18,678
Given his reaction,

199
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:23,882
it seems the mere act of us questioning
the kid is what's sending him into a panic.

200
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:24,990
That's it.

201
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:30,220
I have no other choice.

202
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:33,147
If I die here, they'll
still be able to live.

203
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:36,397
I'm the bomb, so I have to die.

204
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:38,700
With me out of the picture,

205
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:43,373
I know these guys will figure out a
way to defeat that devil and save Mom!

206
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:47,404
It shouldn't be this difficult.

207
00:12:47,780 --> 00:12:50,662
Let's just ask him about
Kosaku Kawajiri already.

208
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:52,240
Hold on, Josuke.

209
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:54,071
Something is up with him.

210
00:12:56,660 --> 00:12:58,240
Hey, what's wrong?

211
00:12:59,000 --> 00:12:59,830
Hey.

212
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:04,650
No!

213
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:05,757
I can't do it!

214
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:08,157
Something's keeping me
from slashing my throat.

215
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:11,757
Wait, what isn't that Kira's? Yeah. It is.

216
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,277
That's a face I'd never forget.

217
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,460
It's deadly queen.

218
00:13:19,420 --> 00:13:22,537
Actually, you're looking at
deadly Queen's bomb type 3.

219
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:25,277
Bites the dust to attack me.

220
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:26,477
Now would be futile.

221
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:30,997
In fact, the only reason you can see me is
because I've already entered your pupils.

222
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:34,300
It doesn't matter how
many of you have gathered.

223
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:35,930
together.

224
00:13:36,013 --> 00:13:39,560
The moment you asked about my true
identity, your fate was sealed.

225
00:13:56,260 --> 00:13:57,300
Oh, Hiato.

226
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:58,997
I guess you're already awake.

227
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:01,377
I'm glad you finally decided to answer me,

228
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:04,517
but there's no need to scream
this early in the morning.

229
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:05,677
Breakfast is ready.

230
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:06,701
Come and get it.

231
00:14:13,180 --> 00:14:15,980
I tried, but I couldn't stop him.

232
00:14:16,340 --> 00:14:17,700
He got them too.

233
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:20,800
It doesn't matter what I do now.

234
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:21,820
In one hour,

235
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,017
fate will run its course and Rohan and his

236
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:26,117
friends will be wiped out
the face of the earth.

237
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:27,030
It's over.

238
00:14:27,113 --> 00:14:28,019
It's all my fault.

239
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:30,300
I can't even kill myself.

240
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,017
Well, if I died,

241
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:34,077
he wouldn't be able to use his power,

242
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:36,940
but Bites the Dust is
programmed to protect me.

243
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:39,757
He's unstoppable!

244
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:41,640
Yoshikage Kira is a monster!

245
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:47,271
Unless he dies or decides to shut off
Bites the Dust at just the right time,

246
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:49,837
those guys are going to be blown sky high!

247
00:14:49,920 --> 00:14:51,520
He's made sure of it!

248
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:12,335
He either has to die or shut off bites
the dust at just the right moment

249
00:15:13,640 --> 00:15:16,997
It's crazy I never thought
I'd ever be capable

250
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:19,904
of something like killing
a person in cold blood

251
00:15:20,180 --> 00:15:25,880
I mean, I'm a puny 11-year-old kid What
could I do against a monster like him?

252
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:28,760
A monster

253
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:30,510
That's it?

254
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:35,347
Eleven years old or not, there's one
thing I can use to take him down for good.

255
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:39,392
Kira called me his secret weapon earlier.

